## Summary † (write last)

*Plain language, readable without the rest of the protocol; every technical
term gets a half-sentence gloss on first use (wikilink in addition, never
instead).*

- **Question †:** <the same sentence as in the Intent>
- **Did †:** <what was done, one sentence — for a reader with no context>
- **Result †:** <number(s) + run_id — no number that is absent below>
- **Status †:** <on track | blocked by <what> | needs a decision on <what>>

## Intent (before the run)

- **Question / hypothesis:** <the one question — what do we expect?>
- **Success / failure criterion:** <how do we recognise whether it worked?
  One id per promise to the code — [K1] per conjunct — each reappearing as
  a lowercase key in the reportable run's metrics.json (→ §2.A1)>
- **Stop rule:** <at what point do we abandon the direction — fixed
  upfront; [S1] per rule (→ §2.A1)>
- **Registered fork:** <if a precondition decides which of two questions the
  run answers, register the fork BEFORE the run: condition + question per
  branch, [W1] per fork (→ §2.A10, §2.A1); "n/a" if there is only one outcome>
- **Type:** <exploratory (generates hypotheses, none of it reported as a
  test) | confirmatory (tests a hypothesis fixed before the run)>
- **Timebox:** <hard budget, e.g. 4h — then log and ask>
- **Split touched:** <which split may be touched: train | dev | test>
- **Preflight audit:** <date · scope sha · N findings (blockers fixed /
  accepted with reason / dismissed with reason) — the code-vs-intent audit
  that runs after the instrument check and before freezing (→ §2.A12)>
- **Frozen before run:** no *(to "yes" only after the instrument check)*
- **Why this design †:** <choice of model, dataset, method — one sentence>
- **Rival explanations †:** <per confound: what OTHER than the hypothesis
  produces the same number · error direction (does it push for or against
  the hypothesis?) · the check as CODE in evaluate() (→ §2.D5)>
- **Out of scope †:** <the neighbouring questions this run leaves open>

## Result (after the run — write back, don't go quiet)

- **Answer to the question:** <number(s) + run_id, produced by
  `analysis/<note>.py --check`, never retyped; long form → [[note]]>
- **Raw output:** <one real prompt+answer pair per finding>
- **Interpretation / next step:** <one sentence; keep instrument findings
  apart from findings about the subject>
- **Outcome †:** <expected or surprising — failures belong here>
- **Rival check †:** <which rivals are ruled out, which still stand?>
- **Caps/drops †:** <what was omitted or limited>
- **Analysis audit †:** <date · scope sha · N findings — the audit of the
  EVALUATION against the frozen criterion, before the number leaves
  (→ §2.D11)>

